{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909988-duration-for-iron-edict-for-bonded-retainers","id":909988,"title":"Duration for iron edict for bonded retainers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T05:26:50-07:00","id":909988,"title":"Duration for iron edict for bonded retainers","content":"On p. 100 is written, that disciplines endure longer for thralls in blood bond 3:<br /> <br /> &quot; Lastly, all of the regnant\u2019s lingering Discipline effects gain <br /> additional duration. Any Discipline that would last a scene lasts <br /> one night. Any that last a night instead last a week. One week <br /> becomes one month. One month becomes one year. &quot;<br /> <br /> For the iron edict is written, that it last\u00b4s until the next sunrise:<br /> <br /> &quot;Many Kindred use <br /> Iron Edict to issue a simple command, such as \u201cObey my direct <br /> instructions when I give them to you,\u201d which effectively gives <br /> them control over the minion until the sun comes up \u2014 though <br /> it doesn\u2019t extend the duration of the Mesmerized Condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Does this mean, that it lasts for people in bb3 one week?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:07:08-07:00","id":910119,"title":"","content":"Yes, I would say it does. I would also say it extends the duration of the Mesmerised condition from a scene to a night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:45:43-07:00","id":910187,"title":"","content":"So, you could turn a retainer with BB3 into an obedient slave by casting iron edict with a suggestion like &quot;\u201cObey my direct <br /> instructions when I give them to you,\u201d as mentioned in the rules. ... He wouldn\u00b4t remember what he did during this week, because of the Dominated condition ... But you could tell him a plausible story about what happened and then renew the iron edict. .... Even after years in this state he would still not remember his slavery after the last iron edict would be resolved ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:47:34-07:00","id":910190,"title":"","content":"Better yet, use The Lying Mind to give him false memories of what happened during the week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:29:12-07:00","id":910458,"title":"","content":"Just going to throw this out there.. But if your retainer is BB3 ... he is already an obedient willing slave who thinks you can do no wrong because he is in love with you. most who are BB3 if you say jump.. They ask &quot;how high?&quot; Not sure why you would need to dominate them. Hurting you (physically and emotionally ) is a breaking point -5 / humanity 1 .. Most people BB3 cant even imagine standing up and saying No to their Regnant. <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; Has someone\u2019s name alone make you bite your<br /> lower lip in anticipation? Has it ever aroused you to imagine<br /> her reaction to something you\u2019ve done? Have you ever sabotaged<br /> something that could have been special, for fear of its intrusion<br /> between you and her? Has your brain gone wild, imagining the<br /> worst possible scenario when she meets someone new? Have you<br /> ever thought to intervene in order to protect what you have?<br /> Have you ever tried to agitate her, because her irritation is better<br /> than her neglect? This is the feeling of a full blood bond. It\u2019s<br /> nothing short of infatuation. It\u2019s a tantalizing, forceful affection<br /> that always eats at the back of your mind. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:32:39-07:00","id":910552,"title":"","content":"Sure, but people under the effects of such profound obsession are unpredictable and potentially dangerous. Dominated servants are far safer and more reliable. Besides, why take the chance that your thrall might screw up by leaving them the opportunity to interpret your instructions for themselves? Seems like an unnecessary risk that could be avoided by simply insuring they have no choice but to carry out your commands to the letter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:36:53-07:00","id":910990,"title":"","content":"I think it really depends on how you nurture the relationship of the one Bonded. I feel that if BB3 weren't super safe and reliable servants, There would be more stories of ghouls harming their masters. Vampires depend on their ghouls for daytime care, they are loyal and reliable, which comes from the blood bond. Again, I think it would only be dangerous if you never paid attention to them, and they couldn't get their fix of you. Ghouls can end up spending centuries with their masters under BB3. If they were volatile dangerous things, I am not sure vampires would have them...<br /> <br /> Permanently Dominated servants are far more mindless. Unable to form new memories. Unable to think for themselves or deviate from the plan should something unforeseen happen. Unable to learn from mistakes, because they couldn't remember making them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:47:37-07:00","id":911761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909988-duration-for-iron-edict-for-bonded-retainers?p=910990#post910990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it really depends on how you nurture the relationship of the one Bonded. I feel that if BB3 weren't super safe and reliable servants, There would be more stories of ghouls harming their masters. Vampires depend on their ghouls for daytime care, they are loyal and reliable, which comes from the blood bond. Again, I think it would only be dangerous if you never paid attention to them, and they couldn't get their fix of you. Ghouls can end up spending centuries with their masters under BB3. If they were volatile dangerous things, I am not sure vampires would have them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, I actually agree with you. Sorry, my post was meant to be from the perspective of a detatched Ventrue or other master of Dominate. In retrospect I really didn't say anything to indicate that I meant it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/909988-duration-for-iron-edict-for-bonded-retainers?p=910990#post910990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permanently Dominated servants are far more mindless. Unable to form new memories. Unable to think for themselves or deviate from the plan should something unforeseen happen. Unable to learn from mistakes, because they couldn't remember making them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Though, a jaded and long-lived vampire who has grown accustomed to being able to effortlessly supplant their servants' will with their own might undervalue that ability and overvalue their own ability to plan ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}